{
  "name": "Last Mile L1: The Weight You Carry",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-sandals-tan.webp",
  "system": {
    "category": "technique",
    "source": "Bad Eden Bulwark + Shadow Courier v1.0 (RFI-native rules)",
    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Nobody stays behind.</em></p><p><strong>Mode: Psychopomp / drift: Sideways.</strong></p><p>Your default Package type is a <strong>Soul</strong> — a specific character, creature, or intangible (a secret, a confession, a deathbed wish, a refugee's name, an unfinished obligation) that cannot reach safety on its own.</p><p><strong>While carrying a Soul:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Your movement speed is <strong>reduced by 1 square</strong>, but allies traveling with you gain <strong>+1 square of movement speed</strong> (the Soul's witness-weight pulls them forward).</p></li><li><p>You <strong>reroll the lowest die</strong> on Stealth (Intrigue) and Athletics (Violence) checks made specifically to <strong>protect or conceal the Soul</strong> (not all stealth/athletics — just protective acts).</p></li></ul><p><strong>On delivery:</strong> When you successfully deliver a Soul to safety (the GM confirms the destination counts as safety for that Soul), the recipient Domain gains <strong>+1 Loyalty marks</strong> and <strong>Darkness in the recipient's hex is reduced by 1 point</strong>.</p><p>You may receive a new Soul any time your Package slot is empty.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
